  "method": [
    "Imagine the Internet as a vast library where every book is stored under its unique address.",
    "When you type a URL, it’s like asking for a specific book. The internet uses something called Domain Name System (DNS) to find that exact location in the library.",
    "Caching helps by storing frequently accessed pages locally on your device so they don’t have to be fetched from servers every time. It’s like having a personal copy of those books nearby.",
